1
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:12,140
Plan A costs 20 dollars a month, plus 3 dollars per gigabyte.

2
00:00:12,190 --> 00:00:17,210
Plan B costs 8 dollars a month, plus 5 dollars per gigabyte.

3
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:23,640
For g gigabytes, the plans cost the same when 20 plus 3 g equals 8 plus 5 g.

4
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:24,130
Find g.

5
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:27,750
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,890
The unknown is on both sides.

7
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:33,660
Take away the smaller amount, 3 g, from both sides.

8
00:00:33,710 --> 00:00:36,650
That leaves 20 equals 8 plus 2 g.

9
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:38,790
Subtract 8: 12 equals 2 g.

10
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:40,760
Divide by 2: g equals 6.

11
00:00:40,810 --> 00:00:44,680
Both plans cost the same for 6 gigabytes.

12
00:00:44,730 --> 00:00:49,810
Remember: to solve 3 x plus 5 equals 26, undo the operations.

13
00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:52,000
Subtract 5: 3 x equals 21.

14
00:00:52,050 --> 00:00:54,570
Divide by 3: x equals 7.

15
00:00:54,620 --> 00:01:00,160
Do the same thing to both sides at every step, like keeping a balance level.

16
00:01:00,210 --> 00:01:04,610
When the unknown is on both sides, remove it from one side first.

17
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:09,000
Usually take away the term with the smaller coefficient.

18
00:01:09,050 --> 00:01:09,790
Your turn.

19
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:12,070
Solve 9 x equals 4 x plus 35.

20
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:15,590
Pause the video and try it.

21
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:19,250
Subtract 4 x from both sides: 5 x equals 35.

22
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:21,790
Divide by 5: x equals 7.

23
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:25,080
If there are brackets, expand them first.

24
00:01:25,130 --> 00:01:33,030
4, bracket, x minus 3, equals 2, bracket, x plus 5, becomes 4 x minus 12 equals 2 x plus 10.

25
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:36,700
Subtract 2 x: 2 x minus 12 equals 10.

26
00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:38,890
Add 12: 2 x equals 22.

27
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:40,930
So x equals 11.

28
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:42,320
Here is the method.

29
00:01:42,370 --> 00:01:44,910
Step 1: expand any brackets.

30
00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:51,740
Step 2: collect the unknowns on one side, by subtracting the smaller x term from both sides.

31
00:01:51,790 --> 00:01:55,500
Step 3: collect the numbers on the other side.

32
00:01:55,550 --> 00:02:00,580
Step 4: divide to find x, then check it in the original equation.

33
00:02:00,630 --> 00:02:03,930
Solve 2 x plus 11 equals 5 x plus 26.

34
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:09,200
Subtract 2 x from both sides: 11 equals 3 x plus 26.

35
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:12,190
Subtract 26: negative 15 equals 3 x.

36
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:14,940
Divide by 3: x equals negative 5.

37
00:02:14,990 --> 00:02:17,650
Negative answers are fine.

38
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:20,920
Solve 2, bracket, x plus 6, equals 30.

39
00:02:20,970 --> 00:02:25,260
One way is to expand: 2 x plus 12 equals 30.

40
00:02:25,310 --> 00:02:25,920
Your turn.

41
00:02:25,970 --> 00:02:27,330
Finish it: what is x?

42
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:30,200
Pause and work it out.

43
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:32,830
Subtract 12: 2 x equals 18.

44
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:35,170
Divide by 2: x equals 9.

45
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:40,010
Check: 9 plus 6 is 15, and 2 times 15 is 30.

46
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:45,870
The angles of a triangle are x, 2 x plus 10, and 3 x minus 10 degrees.

47
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:48,010
They add up to 180.

48
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:53,130
The 10s cancel out, so 6 x equals 180, and x equals 30.

49
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:57,120
The angles are 30, 70 and 80 degrees.

50
00:02:57,170 --> 00:03:00,480
Kai solves 6 x minus 5 equals 2 x plus 15.

51
00:03:00,530 --> 00:03:03,280
Which line goes wrong first?

52
00:03:03,330 --> 00:03:04,560
Line 1 is wrong.

53
00:03:04,610 --> 00:03:08,720
Subtracting 2 x from both sides gives 6 x minus 2 x.

54
00:03:08,770 --> 00:03:12,390
Adding 5 to both sides gives 15 plus 5.

55
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:15,730
So 4 x equals 20, and x equals 5.

56
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:19,530
Businesses solve this kind of equation all the time.

57
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:21,660
A school club makes T-shirts.

58
00:03:21,710 --> 00:03:30,340
It pays 60 dollars for the printing screen, plus 4 dollars for each shirt, and sells each shirt for 10 dollars.

59
00:03:30,390 --> 00:03:33,910
It breaks even when 60 plus 4 N equals 10 N.

60
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:37,800
That gives 6 N equals 60, so N equals 10 shirts.

61
00:03:37,850 --> 00:03:41,520
After that, every shirt makes a profit.

62
00:03:41,570 --> 00:03:42,900
One last question.

63
00:03:42,950 --> 00:03:45,510
Solve x plus 13 equals 4 x plus 1.

64
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:48,990
Pause the video and answer.

65
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:53,230
Subtract x from both sides: 13 equals 3 x plus 1.

66
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:55,480
Subtract 1: 12 equals 3 x.

67
00:03:55,530 --> 00:03:57,240
So x equals 4.

68
00:03:57,290 --> 00:04:00,490
To remember: expand any brackets first.

69
00:04:00,540 --> 00:04:05,130
Get the unknown on one side by subtracting the smaller term.

70
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:08,380
Do the same to both sides at every step.

71
00:04:08,430 --> 00:04:12,060
And check the answer in the original equation.

72
00:04:12,110 --> 00:04:17,190
Great work! Now practise lesson 2.5 on Camday.
